# Loaded by Vite for `npm run build` (mode=production).
#
# RELATIVE on purpose. vercel.json rewrites /api/* to the Render service, so
# the browser only ever talks to the origin it is already on.
#
# Going straight to https://<backend>.onrender.com works in a plain Chrome and
# fails in ways that are miserable to diagnose everywhere else: it is a
# cross-site request carrying a third-party cookie, which Brave's Shields
# block outright, Safari's tracking prevention drops, and Chrome is in the
# middle of phasing out. The symptom is not an error — the request never
# leaves the browser, DevTools shows "provisional headers", and the server
# logs show nothing at all because nothing ever arrived.
#
# Through the proxy it is same-origin: no CORS preflight, no third-party
# cookie, and nothing for a shield to object to.
#
# A VITE_API_URL set in the host's environment still overrides this.
VITE_API_URL=/api
